			"Message": "chore(deps): update Queue submodule to latest commit\n\n- Updates the Queue dependency submodule to commit a49ab4e8e9518c5b4284fc30fa71801b9c7d04d0\n- Maintains compatibility with Land's IPC and process management systems that rely on Queue for asynchronous task handling\n- Ensures access to latest performance optimizations and stability improvements in the Queue library, which is critical for Mountain's runtime environment and Cocoon's extension host communication\n- Part of ongoing dependency hygiene to support Land's goals of reduced memory usage and reliable cross-process coordination",
			"SHA": "fa49a02443df97cca95235a22a0d6a55f92b820a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-10T14:34:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				25,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(license): Migrate from CC0 1.0 to Land Public License v1.0\n\nReplaced Creative Commons Zero license with custom Land Public License (LPL-1.0) to establish project-specific governance framework. The new license:\n- Implements copyleft requirements for Land project modifications while allowing combination with external works under different licenses\n- Explicitly separates LPL-covered components from external dependencies in combined works\n- Includes patent grants and defensive termination clauses\n- Specifies Bulgarian jurisdiction for dispute resolution\n- Maintains compatibility with permissive licenses (MIT/Apache) while outlining GPL/AGPL interaction\n- Formalizes contribution requirements and source code distribution obligations\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Changes license terms from public domain dedication to reciprocal copyleft structure. All contributors must now comply with LPL-1.0 requirements for distribution and modification.",
			"SHA": "935706d3ead23f9f519b20e51b3bbe8045e0f43b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-05-10T10:10:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				25,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Dependency): update Queue submodule to latest commit\n\n- Updates Queue dependency to commit 2dea26b which includes critical fixes for asynchronous task prioritization\n- Aligns with Land's performance optimization goals by improving background task scheduling in Mountain's process management layer\n- Ensures compatibility with recent changes in Vine IPC protocol handling for RPC command queuing between Cocoon and Mountain\n- Part of ongoing maintenance to leverage upstream improvements in resource-efficient concurrency primitives used in Track dispatcher",
			"SHA": "330f673647f0aeb1125d0053b3529923322af083"
		},
